# File: tests/features/provider-usage.feature
# Generated from: specs/40-show-provider-plan-usage-in-the-routed-status-line-and-usage/requirements.md
Feature: Show provider plan usage in the routed status line and /usage

  @SCN001
  Scenario: The status line shows the selected provider's usage windows
    Given an OpenCode Go model is selected and its usage reading reports 5h, weekly and monthly windows
    When a routed main-loop step completes
    Then the status line shows the model, the thinking level and "5h", "weekly" and "monthly" with whole-number percents in that order

  @SCN002
  Scenario: Switching providers switches the usage shown
    Given the status line shows OpenCode Go's usage windows
    When the person selects an xAI model and a routed main-loop step completes while an OpenCode Go usage read is still running
    Then the status line shows no OpenCode Go windows, even after that read finishes

  @SCN003
  Scenario: A provider without a usage source shows no usage
    Given a ClinePass model is selected
    When a routed main-loop step completes
    Then the status line shows the model and thinking level only
    And no usage request is sent

  @SCN004
  Scenario: Usage endpoint reads are throttled per provider and account
    Given OpenCode Go's usage endpoint was read 30 seconds ago for the active account
    When another OpenCode Go main-loop step completes
    Then no usage request is sent and the status line shows the kept windows
    And a step completing 60 seconds after that read sends one usage request

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Codex usage comes from response headers
    Given an OpenAI Codex routed response carries x-codex-primary and x-codex-secondary rate-limit headers
    When that routed main-loop step completes
    Then the status line shows the "5h" and "7d" windows from those headers
    And no request is sent to the Codex usage endpoint

  @SCN006
  Scenario: A failed usage read never affects the routed step
    Given OpenCode Go's usage endpoint answers HTTP 500
    When a routed main-loop step completes
    Then the step's answer is unchanged
    And the status line shows the model and thinking level with the last good windows or none

  @SCN007
  Scenario: The routed error line keeps its text
    Given a routed main-loop step fails with an error kind
    When the status line is updated
    Then it reads "<model> · <provider> error: <kind>" with no usage windows

  @SCN008
  Scenario: A Claude model clears the line
    Given the status line shows OpenCode Go's usage windows
    When a Claude main-loop step runs
    Then the status line is cleared
    And no provider usage request is sent

  @SCN009
  Scenario: /usage lists every logged-in provider after the built-in command
    Given stored logins for OpenCode Go, OpenAI Codex and xAI, and none for ClinePass
    When the person runs /usage
    Then the built-in usage command runs unchanged
    And nmg-router's output lists OpenAI Codex, OpenCode Go and xAI in that order with window lines such as "5h 23% · resets in 2h 10m"
    And xAI shows "No usage reading available" and ClinePass has no entry

  @SCN010
  Scenario: One failing provider does not hide the others in /usage
    Given stored logins for OpenCode Go and OpenAI Codex, and OpenAI Codex's usage read answers HTTP 500
    When the person runs /usage
    Then OpenAI Codex's entry reads "Usage could not be read: unavailable"
    And OpenCode Go's entry shows its windows

  @SCN011
  Scenario: /usage with no provider logins adds nothing
    Given no login-requiring provider has a stored login
    When the person runs /usage
    Then only the built-in usage command's result is returned

  @SCN012
  Scenario: Credentials never appear in usage output
    Given a provider usage read that sends a sentinel credential
    When the status line and /usage output are produced and a usage failure is reported
    Then the sentinel appears in no status text, /usage output, log line or store write
